editorialMd:
The working idea

For each lowercase word, consider each of its nonempty prefixes and count how many input words begin with that prefix, including repeated words and the word itself. Produce the sum of these counts for each word in input order.

Return the weighted sum of the derived sequence: multiply its first value by 1, its second by 2, and so on, then add the products. Return 0 for an empty sequence.

Why this works

Each derived value follows the unit's stated order and includes exactly the items allowed by its definition. The receipt then folds or filters those values without changing their meaning. Check the empty, singleton, repeated and maximum-size inputs before trusting the final total.

Target time O(total characters); space O(n).

javascript
function prefixCabinetBossReceipt(words, k) {
  const a=words; let out=[];
  const next=[new Map()],counts=[0];for(const word of a){let node=0;for(const c of word){if(!next[node].has(c)){next[node].set(c,next.length);next.push(new Map());counts.push(0);}node=next[node].get(c);counts[node]++;}}for(const word of a){let node=0,s=0;for(const c of word){node=next[node].get(c);s+=counts[node];}out.push(s);}
  return out.reduce((s,x,i)=>s+(i+1)*x,0);
}


